<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">30 November in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">6 events that happened on 30 November, from 1016 to 1995.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/edmund-ironside" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/edmund-ironside.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1016">1016 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">1,010 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Edmund Ironside dies, leaving Cnut king of all England</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Edmund II died weeks after agreeing to divide <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a> with the Danish king Cnut. Cnut became sole king, later also ruling <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/denmark">Denmark</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norway">Norway</a> in a North Sea empire.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-sea">North Sea</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/denmark">Denmark</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1667">1667 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">359 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Jonathan Swift is born in Dublin</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Jonathan Swift, later Dean of St Patrick's Cathedral in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dublin">Dublin</a>, was born. His Gulliver's Travels and A Modest Proposal made him one of the great satirists in English.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1835">1835 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">191 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Samuel Clemens, later Mark Twain, is born</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mark-twain">Samuel Langhorne Clemens</a> was born in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/florida">Florida</a>, Missouri. As Mark Twain he wrote The Adventures of Tom Sawyer and Adventures of Huckleberry Finn, drawing on his boyhood on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mississippi-river">Mississippi</a>.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1872">1872 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">154 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Scotland and England play the first international football match</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a> drew 0-0 at Hamilton Crescent in Partick, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/glasgow">Glasgow</a>, before about 4,000 spectators. It is recognised by FIFA as the first official international football match.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1939">1939 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">87 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Soviet Union invades Finland</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Soviet forces attacked <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/finland">Finland</a>, starting the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/winter-war">Winter War</a>. Fierce Finnish resistance inflicted heavy losses before Finland ceded territory in March 1940, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/red-army">Red Army</a>'s poor showing was noted in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berlin">Berlin</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/finland">Finland</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1995">1995 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">31 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Bill Clinton becomes the first US president to visit Northern Ireland</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Bill Clinton addressed crowds in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belfast">Belfast</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/derry">Derry</a> in support of the peace process. The visit added momentum to the talks that produced the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/good-friday-agreement">Good Friday Agreement</a> in 1998.</p></div></li></ol>
